speechtext:
May I interrupt my hon. friend for a moment? I should have cleared that up with the hon. member for Cape Breton South. This is not a board of appeal;
Demobilization-Army

it is a departmental board of review. I made it clear that the board proceeds on the assumption that the court-martial proceedings were properly taken, that the proceedings were regular and that the sentence imposed was in accordance with the law. There is no rehearing of evidence; there is no submission of new facts. It is a board of review, just as the remission branch of the Department of Justice reviews the sentence of a prisoner on the assumption that it is a regular sentence; and it is for that reason that there is no public hearing and no representative of outside groups.
